# ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md — append these sections

These are project-agnostic instructions that apply to every Claude Code session on your machine. Append them to your existing `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, or create the file from scratch if you don't have one.


---

## Code research: the project's tool, not agents

Search code with the project's chosen tool (`tools.code_research` in the bound configuration), never with an Explore agent or any other agent, whatever a skill recommends.

<!-- TOGGLE:code_research:findwright START -->
- FindWright's own guidance (`~/.claude/rules/findwright.md`, which `/findwright:setup` installs) holds the lookup sequence. Without FindWright on this computer, use Grep, Glob and Read.
<!-- TOGGLE:code_research:findwright END -->
<!-- TOGGLE:code_research:none START -->
- This project has no code-research tool: the `/find` skill holds the Grep, Glob and Read sequence. Read the sources directly instead of starting an agent.
<!-- TOGGLE:code_research:none END -->
<!-- TOGGLE:code_research:custom START -->
- Before any code research, use **{{TOOLS_CODE_RESEARCH_NAME}}** ({{TOOLS_CODE_RESEARCH_URL}}) per the project's `/find` skill, and refine `~/.claude/hooks/{{TOOLS_CODE_RESEARCH_NAME_KEBAB}}-first.py`'s `SEQUENCE_BULLETS` constant if the bind step's stub is too generic for your tool.
- Fall back to agents only when {{TOOLS_CODE_RESEARCH_NAME}} is unavailable for the scope you need.
<!-- TOGGLE:code_research:custom END -->
